From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: The scale of each monitor, recommended and changed on the fly.

As in Windows 10, every monitor has a scale of its own: recommended from
its size (EDID) and resolution, about 110 pixels an inch taken as 100 %,
and moved some steps from there by the user, which is kept in
HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop\PerMonitorSettings\<monitor>\DpiValue. The
monitor's source gets the DPI; the primary one's goes to LogPixels too,
the system DPI of the processes to come.

DisplayConfigGetDeviceInfo and DisplayConfigSetDeviceInfo read and set
it with the types Windows' Settings use (GET/SET_SOURCE_DPI_SCALE). A new
scale applies at once, without a restart: every process reads the
monitors again, the server gives every window its monitor's new DPI,
and every toplevel window hears of it in its own thread
(WM_WINE_DPICHANGED). A window that knows its monitor's DPI gets
WM_DPICHANGED with a rectangle that keeps its size in its own terms
(and its children WM_DPICHANGED_BEFOREPARENT/AFTERPARENT in v2); any
other window keeps its coordinates and is drawn again at the new scale;
maximized windows take the maximized place again.
---
